Found in read-only bug hunt (langertha-reviewer, 2026-09-25). REPRODUCED offline (vLLM engine chat_response, think_tag_filter default on).

lib/Langertha/Role/ThinkTag.pm:83-89 (filter_think_content), applied by around chat_response on every engine.

1) Orphan closing tag: chat templates of DeepSeek-R1 and Qwen3-thinking put the opening <think> into the generation prompt, so a server without a reasoning parser returns "reasoning...\n</think>\n\nAnswer". Only matched pairs and an unclosed OPENING tag are handled. Repro: content "Let me think about it.\n</think>\n\nThe answer is 4." -> content unchanged (reasoning + stray </think> in content), thinking undef.
   Fix: if no opening tag is present but a closing tag is, treat everything before the first </tag> as thinking.
2) Unconditional trim: s/^\s+// and s/\s+$// run even when no tag was found, so every response on every engine is altered. Repro: "    def f():\n        return 1\n" -> "def f():\n        return 1" (first-line indentation of code/indented markdown lost).
   Fix: only trim the whitespace adjacent to removed tag blocks, and return the Response untouched (no clone_with) when no tag matched.
3) Minor: nested <think>a<think>b</think>c</think>done -> content "c</think>done", thinking "a<think>b"; tag match is case-sensitive (<Think> passes through). Low priority, note only.
Also: chunk_callback receives the raw <think> text during streaming; only the final aggregate is filtered (by design today, worth a POD line).

